      children: "The JavaScript event loop stands as one of the language's most fundamental and consequential mechanisms, directly shaping application performance, user experience, and code reliability. Its elegant design-coordinating asynchronous operations through a single-threaded event-driven model-enables the rich, interactive web applications that define the modern internet. Yet this elegance comes with complexity, requiring developers to think carefully about execution timing, task prioritization, and the myriad ways asynchronous operations can interact and interfere."
